    "All three estimator families (Callaway-Sant'Anna, Sun-Abraham, Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess) eliminate forbidden comparisons by construction and accommodate unrestricted treatment-effect heterogeneity; treatment-effect homogeneity is no longer a substantive assumption.",
    "Callaway-Sant'Anna is identified as the modal default/off-the-shelf heterogeneity-robust estimator, with Sun-Abraham commonly used as a companion for event-study specifications and Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess emerging as the efficiency-oriented choice.",
    "No-anticipation is a maintained assumption across all three estimators, though each accommodates anticipation via parameter choices (CS: anticipation horizon; SA/BJS: dropping leads, model restrictions).",
